{"url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/eleceng", "final_url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/eleceng", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Skip to main content\nSEARCH\nLOGIN\nABOUT\nACADEMICS\nADMISSIONS\nRESEARCH\nSTUDENT AFFAIRS\nSUPPORT CCNY\nELECTRICAL ENGINEERING\nHOME\nABOUT US\nUNDERGRADUATE PROGRAM\nGRADUATE PROGRAMS\nNEWS & EVENTS\nCONTACT US\nHome\n/\nThe Grove School of Engineering\n/\nElectrical Engineering\nWelcome to the Department of Electrical Engineering\nA quick look at essential statistics that define our Electrical Engineering department.\n450+\nUndergraduate, graduate, and PhD students enrolled in the Electrical Engineering program\n25+\nFaculty members in the Electrical Engineering Department\n100+\nPublications produced by the Electrical Engineering Department each year.\n$10M+\nAnnual research funding secured by the Electrical Engineering Department.\nSHAPING TOMORROW'S TECHNOLOGY, TODAY\nExplore the Electrical Engineering Department at CCNY\nThe Electrical Engineering Department at the City College of New York (CCNY) is dedicated to advancing knowledge and innovation in one of the most dynamic fields of engineering. Electrical engineering is a diverse discipline, ranging from the design of the smallest transistors used in computer chips to the development of large-scale communication systems that connect the globe and venture into outer space.\nResearch and Academic Excellence\nOur department leads in lasers, fiber optics, microcomputers, satellite communications, control systems, and signal processing. Faculty are engaged in active research in these fields, offering advanced students hands-on experience in innovative projects.\nComprehensive Degree Programs\nWe offer accredited degree programs at the undergraduate, master's, and doctoral levels, preparing students for successful careers in electrical engineering and related fields. Our curriculum is designed to provide a strong foundation in both theoretical knowledge and practical skills, ensuring our graduates are well-equipped to meet the challenges of today\u2019s technological landscape.\nFaculty Spotlight:\nTushar Jois\nTushar Jois is an Assistant Professor of Electrical Engineering at the City College of New York and a member of the doctoral faculty of computer science at the CUNY Graduate Center.\nRead More\nResearch Spotlight:\nAI-Driven Cardiovascular Diagnosis\nA City College of New York-led project is developing a low-cost, easy-to-use, and high-precision system for early cardiovascular disease diagnosis using AI/ML technologies.\nRead More\nContact Information\nProf. Fred Moshary, Department Chair\nSteinman Hall\nRoom 602\n160 Convent Avenue\nNew York, NY 10031\np: 212.650.7248\nf: 212.650.8249\ne: eechair@ccny.cuny.edu\nReady To Apply\nCity College\u2019s Electrical Engineering undergraduate program provides students with the foundational technical skills needed to excel in a rapidly evolving field, shaping the future of technology and innovation.\nApply Undergraduate\nCity College\u2019s Electrical Engineering graduate programs equip students with advanced technical expertise and research skills to lead and innovate in the ever-expanding world of electrical and electronic technology.\nApply Graduate\nElectrical Engineering Useful Links\nFaculty\nResearch Overview\nEngineering Alumni\nDonations\nSocial Media Links\nTwitter\nMastodon\nThreads\nBlueSky\nInstagram\nFacebook\nWe use cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience on our website, analyze our website traffic, and understand where our visitors are coming from. If you choose \"ACCEPT ALL\", you consent to the use of all cookies. You can accept and reject individual cookie types and revoke your consent for the future at any time at \"Settings\".\nPrivacy policy\nAbout us\nCOOKIE SETTINGS\nDENY ALL\nACCEPT ALL\nThe City College of New York\n160 Convent Avenue New York, NY 10031\np: 212.650.7000\nSTUDENTS\nEmail\nAcademic Cale